# DEFORM-FIELD: the deformation field around the main view (Notion DEFORM-ARCH card 1). A script presses the
# DeformStamp asset DS_CircleRim three times along a line in FIELD_Barn; the debug view "Deformation Field" shows the
# field over the ground only (blue = sink, red = rim; the shading word's LANDSCAPE bit, grass keeps the grey). The camera then moves 30 m: the clipmap scrolls (toroidal, texel
# snapped to the unjittered view) and the prints stay on their world spots, read from L1 where L0 no longer covers.
# NEEDS the DesertCtl `lua` op (REMAINDER): it runs the text through a ScriptEngine under the open scene's WorldContext.
Дано run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Deformation Field"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,400,150
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,-0.94,-0.35
Когда lua "for i = 0, 2 do World.deform{ Stamp = 'DS_CircleRim', At = vector.create(-150 + i * 150, 0, 0), Params = { Radius = 30 } } end"
Тогда-вид 1_stamp from 4 m above, three round prints in a row on the ground, 1.5 m apart, each a blue sink ringed by a red rim, large; no speckle of grass over them (grass pixels stay grey); editor.log errors 0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 800,400,150
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.88,-0.44,-0.165
Тогда-вид 2_scrolled_l0 the camera moved 8 m to the side (the L0 window scrolled, still covering the row): the same three prints at the same world spots on the checker, no shift and no second copy; editor.log errors 0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 3000,1500,150
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.893,-0.447,-0.045
Тогда-вид 3_scrolled_l1 from 30 m to the side (outside L0's 20.48 m half-window, read from L1 at 8 cm/texel): the same three prints at the same world spots, coarser, on the darker L1 grey; editor.log errors 0
